      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It checks that the Base58 error-message format string is not a valid Base58 string (it contains characters like spaces, `:`, `%`, `0`, `x` that are excluded from the alphabet). I'll improve readability by using meaningful names, extracting the string into a named variable, and adding a descriptive assertion message.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version uses meaningful variable names (`codec`, `invalidCharErrorFormat`, `isValidBase58`), adds a comment explaining why the error-message format string is not valid Base58, and includes a descriptive assertion message — all while preserving the exact same method call and expected outcome."
